  "created": "2025-01-10T05:25:41.353Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I'd like to suggest changing how avatars that exceed the bounding box limit are ranked. Right now, they're automatically marked as \"Very Poor,\" but I think they should be marked as \"Medium\" instead. Here's why:\n\n1) Avatars that are \"Very Poor\" only because of the bounding box still show up, even when people have settings to hide \"Very Poor\" avatars. Changing them to \"Medium\" would make the filtering less confusing.\n\n2) With avatar scaling now available, any avatar can be huge, making the bounding box limit feel outdated.\n\n3) If the goal is to stop giant avatars from being fallbacks, marking them as \"Medium\" or \"Poor\" should be enough.",
